Resilience review (2026-10-10)
 - single controller = single etcd member: plan 3 controllers for quorum (e.g. make two workers controller+worker)
 - schedule k0s backup (etcd) to S3 outside GitOps + write a restore runbook
 - control-plane node overloaded (media workload + RWX share-manager share its disk; iowait spikes -> Flux/kyverno/operators "leader election lost"): move media workload off it, ideally separate etcd disk
 - workstation node is a Longhorn replica node and flaps often: every volume degrades/rebuilds on each reboot; exclude it from storage or add a third always-on storage node, consider replica count 2
 - one worker hosts most platform pods (Flux, traefik, authelia, cert-manager, alerting): spread with topologySpread/anti-affinity
 - Longhorn nodeDownPodDeletionPolicy is do-nothing: RWO pods stay Terminating on node loss; set delete-both-statefulset-and-deployment-pod
 - traefik single replica, no PDB: 2 replicas + PDB + spread
 - no dead-man's switch: Watchdog -> blackhole, alertmanager+ntfy on the same node; route Watchdog to an external heartbeat
 - kyverno + longhorn webhooks failurePolicy Fail cover flux-system/longhorn-system/traefik: review exclusions for recovery after full outage
 - Longhorn disk overcommit on workers (200%), check headroom
 - not backed up (re-creatable): logs, traces, jellyfin cache, ollama, trivy

Later (2026-11-11)
 - Move away from k0s: vanilla kubeadm, Talos Linux (immutable OS, upgrades via API) or RKE2. Plus automated stepping of the Kubernetes version (system-upgrade-controller for RKE2/k3s, tuppr or talosctl for Talos; k0s has autopilot today). Run pluto/kubent first to catch removed APIs
 - Kured + automated OS updates on nodes (unattended-upgrades, kured drains and reboots one node at a time). Not needed on Talos: OS image upgrades replace it
 - SOPS + age: understand it before implementing. Flux decrypts natively (decryption.provider: sops on the Kustomization), age private key as a Secret in flux-system, .sops.yaml with creation rules, encrypt only data/stringData
 - OpenBao (open Vault fork) on an external node + External Secrets Operator in the cluster. Must not depend on the cluster to come back up (unseal, storage)
 - Dead-man's switch on an external node: Healthchecks or Gatus. Route the Watchdog alert to it, alert via a path that does not go through the cluster
 - Tetragon (eBPF runtime detection/enforcement, from the Cilium project). Not the same as NeuVector: NeuVector is a full platform (scanning, compliance, admission, L7 firewall, runtime, UI) and overlaps Trivy/Kyverno/Cilium; Tetragon only adds the runtime part. Falco is the closer equivalent
 - Security framework: Kubescape operator (NSA/CIS/MITRE scans, Headlamp plugin) or kube-bench for CIS node checks. Decide what to keep from trivy-operator
 - Container image storage: Harbor proxy cache for all upstream registries, Spegel (P2P between nodes) or Zot (light OCI registry) instead of Dragonfly
 - NetBox (+ netbox-operator for IP claims from CRDs) as source of truth, plus iPXE: netboot.xyz or Matchbox/Tinkerbell for node installs
